BORROW DONE (TOOLBOX CORE, 2026-09-27)

Saying / typing the SHOUT of ANY power, tier or kit you don't hold fires that move right now as a
one-shot. Live in the console and voice (bd_game `toolbox.rs` → `Cmd::Toolbox`, protocol v40).
Sim: bd_sim `powers::chain` (`World::borrow_move` / `World::toolbox`); reading:
`powers::toolbox::MoveIndex::read`.

PRIORITY (per phrase)
  1. HELD: a shout / tier name / incantation of a power you hold (tier versions included) — as ever.
  2. KIT: "<kit name> <move word>" (KIT_DONE).
  3. A power / tier NAME (or anything the lexicon resolves to a GRANT: "power up", "devil fruit")
     → grants, as ever. A name is never a borrow, even if some move also shouts it.
  4. BORROW: the exact shout (normalised: case / punctuation / hyphens ignored) of any move of any
     power, tier or kit → that move. A tier's shout borrows that tier's move at its base effect.
  5. Otherwise the lexicon (constructs, costume summons…).

WHAT A BORROW DOES
- Runs the move's ops for you exactly like its holder would (same aim: the crosshair; host-validated).
- NEVER grants the power, never transforms, never switches tiers: Transform / Tier ops are skipped,
  and a move made ONLY of them is not borrowable at all (not in the index; saying the power's name
  is how you become it). No ascend moment on a borrow — only the move's own `juice`.
- Held context: ops are world ops, so they just work. A move that needs a body (a stand's rush) should
  use a generic op that carries it (`Rush(stand: Some(recipe))`, …); otherwise the presentation draws a
  ghost of the power's `companion` for the beat (PRESENTATION_API.md). A borrowed TimeStop / landing
  slam works for powerless players too (ticked by the toolbox step).
- A Lockout (hack / silence) on you blocks borrowed moves too.

PRICE (the presence-tier SPARKS model; don't hand-tune)
- `powers::chain::move_tier(&MoveDef)` → Tiny / Normal / Big / Titan by what the move does on screen
  (a blink / dash / status is Tiny; a shove / small blast / field / yank Normal; a big blast, long
  trench, restore Big; a time stop / gravity core / radius ≥ 9 or 35+ damage blast Titan; generic
  ops count Normal), lifted by the move's `cost` weight (≥ 8 Normal, ≥ 20 Big, ≥ 40 Titan).
- sparks = SparkTuning.tier[tier] (default Tiny 1 / Normal 2 / Big 3 / Titan 5) + `stale` (1) per
  REPEAT of the same move inside the staleness window (`willpower.stale_window`), capped at the bar.
  Cycling through different moves is always cheaper than spamming one.
- Cast ops inside a move pay the cast pipeline's own presence-tier price (and a cast-only move adds
  nothing on top). Infinite willpower: free.

COOLDOWNS
- Per player, per move: the move's `cooldown` (× cooldown effects of powers you hold), in a fixed
  8-slot table (`Toolbox::cds`, alloc-free, rollback-safe; the slot closest to ready is reused when
  full). Borrowing a held power's move is not possible (held priority), so held cooldowns stay theirs.

GLOBAL MOVE ID
- `MoveRef { power: u16, tier: u8, slot: u8 }`, packed `power << 8 | tier << 4 | slot`
  (`MoveRef::pack / unpack / resolve`). On the wire inside `ToolStep::Move { mv, kit }`.

CHECK YOUR SHOUTS
  cargo run --profile fastrel -p bd_sim --example powers_check -- assets/powers/<file>.ron --coverage phrases.txt
  - "WARN shout X: A keeps it; B loses it" = two moves claim one shout: the earlier file wins. Rename.
  - "WARN shout X ... is another power's NAME" = it will grant that power, never fire your move.
  - Single common words ("smash", "claws", "teleport") are GLOBAL now: anyone saying them fires your
    move. Keep that for moves that truly own the word; otherwise make the shout specific.
Tests: crates/bd_sim/tests/toolbox.rs (borrow / cooldown / staleness / price / never transforms).
